            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis and management of lumbar disk disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-9, 142, 145-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Management of the patient with low back pain need not be particularly confusing, expensive, or invasive. A systematic approach to categorizing this ubiquitous symptom etiologically, followed by appropriate choice of diagnostic imaging techniques and an individualized treatment program, will heighten cost-effectiveness and sharply reduce the demand for surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
